# The compound: the demo map, as a file rather than as C#.
#
# A walled compound with a breach, sandbags, a smoke screen, broken ground, a barricade running
# across one tile, and a rooftop reachable only by ladder. Exercises every traversal kind the
# graph builder knows how to generate. Must stay identical to DemoMaps.Compound() until that
# method is retired — a test holds the two side by side.

map Compound

fill disc 0,0 r 6 floor

# The perimeter wall, one hex column wide. A straight wall on a hex grid is a zigzag: each hex
# on the line contributes its north-west and south-west faces. One face is then knocked out,
# which is the breach everyone will funnel through.
wall solid line 2,-3 to 2,2 nw sw
breach 2,0 sw

# Sandbags, and a hedge you cannot see through but can walk straight past.
wall low hex -2,2 se s
wall low hex -1,1 s
wall screen hex -1,-2 ne

# Broken ground.
fill hexes -4,1 -4,2 -3,1 rubble

# Barricades. The first clips a corner off its tile, so most of it is still standable. The
# second splits its tile in half: crossable, but there is nowhere in it to stand.
chord low 0,3 0-2
chord low 0,-3 0-3

# The rooftop. Too high to jump down from, so the ladder is the only way up or off, and a
# parapet along the north edge gives whoever holds the roof something to fight from.
fill hexes 4,-1 4,0 4,1 5,-1 5,0 layer 1 h 3.5
ladder 4,0@0 4,0@1
wall railing hex 4,1 n nw layer 1
